      "englishTranslation": "Exegesis of 'Tat Tvam Asi' (Part 1 — Refuting 'Atat Tvam Asi'): Madhusūdana confronts Dvaita's famous polemical sandhi-split of Chāndogya 6.8.7—reading 'sa ātmā-atat tvam asi' ('Thou art NOT That!') or construing 'Tat' via companionship/dependence rules from Patañjali's Mahābhāṣya ('Vasantādibhyaṣ ṭhak'). Exposing the grammatical and contextual absurdity of 'atat', he shows how Uddālaka's opening promise ('By knowing One, all becomes known'—ekavijñānena sarva-vijñāna-pratijñā) and the declaration 'All this has That as its very Self (aitadātmyam idam sarvam)' would utterly collapse unless 'Tat tvam asi' affirms absolute non-difference!",
